<PolicyLayout
  title="Research and Medical Disclaimer"
  description="Cloud Peptides publishes research information only — not medical advice. Read the full disclaimer."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
>
  <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is medical advice, a diagnosis, or a treatment recommendation. Content is
    published for research and informational purposes only. Always consult a qualified healthcare
    professional before making any decision related to your health.
  </p>

  <h2>Research use only</h2>
  <p>
    Any research materials referenced or sold on this site are intended for laboratory research use
    only and are not for human consumption. No claims of safety or effectiveness for human use are
    made or implied, on this page or anywhere else on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>How our published claims work</h2>
  <p>
    Every substantive scientific statement published in our research library is reviewed and cited
    to a source before it's published, and each compound page shows the evidence type (human,
    animal, in-vitro, mechanistic, regulatory, and so on) and an evidence-quality rating for the
    claims made about it. This is meant to help you judge how settled a piece of research is — it is
    not a substitute for reading the underlying sources yourself or for professional guidance.
  </p>
  <p>
    Evidence quality, evidence type, and how "settled" the interpretation is are shown as separate,
    independent signals — we don't collapse them into a single verdict, and a claim carrying a
    citation is not the same thing as that claim being proven or endorsed by us.
  </p>

  <h2>Regulatory status varies by compound</h2>
  <p>
    Some compounds discussed on this site have an FDA-approved pharmaceutical product under a
    specific brand name, manufacturer, and formulation. That approval belongs to that specific
    product — it does not extend to independently sourced, compounded, or research-grade material
    describing the same underlying molecule. Each compound's regulatory section documents what we
    could verify; where we found nothing, we say so rather than guessing.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal status is your responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    Laws governing research chemicals and peptides vary by location and change over time. It is your
    responsibility to know and follow the laws that apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe a claim on this site is inaccurate, outdated, or miscited, please tell us —
    <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with the compound and claim in question. We'd rather fix it than
    leave it wrong.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
